{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "All configuration management library functions (U2-U8) will be developed in Go within a self-contained, pure package with zero filesystem or network dependencies, copying and adapting necessary data structures from Fabric's internal config packages.",
    "For U1, read set validation logic in the peer's txvalidator will be enhanced to check data values alongside versions in the read set during validation to detect endorsing peer state tampering.",
    "Standard Hyperledger Fabric Protobuf structures (common.Block, common.Envelope, common.ConfigUpdate, etc.) will be used for input and output representations across all library APIs.",
    "Detached signatures for configuration updates (U3, U4) will produce standard Fabric ConfigSignature structures using Go's crypto package interfaces without depending on local MSP disk storage."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "Development work is performed directly on the standard Hyperledger Fabric Go codebase.",
    "Cryptographic keys and certificate material passed into library functions are pre-parsed or provided as standard Go structs/byte slices.",
    "Comprehensive integration test suites and test fixtures (including prototypical configtx.yaml files and MSP material) are already available in the repository.",
    "A single senior Go software developer with expertise in Fabric internals will execute all tasks."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-1",
      "activity_name": "Architecture, Interface Design, and Library Scaffolding",
      "activity_description": "Design the package interface and internal abstractions for the configtx library and the peer validation extension. Set up package structure without external viper/yaml dependencies.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-2",
      "activity_name": "U1: Peer Read Set Value Tampering Detection and Validation",
      "activity_description": "Extend transaction validation logic (txvalidator) in the peer to include values in the read set comparison during validation and invalidate transactions if an endorsing peer tampered with the read set value.",
      "most_likely_effort": 5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-3",
      "activity_name": "U2: Programmatic Channel Creation and Genesis Block Generation",
      "activity_description": "Implement CreateChannelTx and associated profile configuration structures to generate proto.Equal genesis blocks matching configtxgen output without file/network access.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-4",
      "activity_name": "U3: Detached Signature Generation for Channel Update",
      "activity_description": "Implement standalone library function to sign ChannelUpdate payloads with explicit key parameters and generate detached ConfigSignature structures.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-5",
      "activity_name": "U4: Assemble Signed Config Update Envelope",
      "activity_description": "Implement function to combine a ConfigUpdate transaction payload and a collection of detached signatures into a fully signed Envelope transaction equivalent to 'peer channel update / signtx'.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-6",
      "activity_name": "U5: Batch Size Parameter Channel Update Generator",
      "activity_description": "Implement helper function to generate an unsigned ConfigUpdate transaction modifying the max_message_count batch size setting.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-7",
      "activity_name": "U6: Programmatic Organization ConfigGroup Generation",
      "activity_description": "Implement library function to generate an Organization ConfigGroup directly from in-memory cryptographic material matching the output of 'configtxgen -printOrg'.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-8",
      "activity_name": "U7: Programmatic Config Delta Computation (ComputeUpdate)",
      "activity_description": "Implement standalone logic to compute a ConfigUpdate proto representing the delta between base and modified Config trees, matching 'configtxlator compute_update'.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-9",
      "activity_name": "U8: Consortium Organization Addition Update Generator",
      "activity_description": "Implement library function to add an organization ConfigGroup definition to a named consortium in a system channel configuration and return the unsigned update transaction.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-10",
      "activity_name": "Integration Testing, Verification, and Documentation",
      "activity_description": "Run end-to-end unit and integration tests against proto.Equal expectations and integration test suites for all implemented user stories, and complete API documentation.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 34
  }
}
```

